# Supabase, used only by the /sat trainer (Phase 2 accounts).
#
# This file is a COMMITTED TEMPLATE. Next.js never reads it — copy it to
# .env.local (gitignored) for local development, and set the same two
# variables in Vercel for Production and Preview. Leave the values here blank.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the browser bundle at build time, so only ever
# put the publishable key here. It is designed to be public and every table is
# protected by row level security. Never put the secret (sb_secret_...) or
# legacy service_role key in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable.
#
# Because it is baked in at build time, changing these in Vercel requires a
# redeploy — an existing deployment will not pick them up.
#
# Find both under Project Settings > API Keys in the Supabase dashboard.
# On projects created recently the publishable key (sb_publishable_...) is the
# drop-in replacement for the old anon key: same low privileges, same RLS.
#
# Leave these unset and /sat still works: flashcards stay unlimited, the quiz
# keeps its 10-a-day anonymous limit, and sign-in reports that it isn't
# available yet.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
